<title>QATAR: Qatar lists 18th company on bourse.</title>
<headline>Qatar lists 18th company on bourse.</headline>
<dateline>DOHA 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qatar's bourse said on Tuesday it listed a new company on the Doha Securities Market, raising the number of traded firms to 18.</p>
<p>Al-Ahli Hospital Company Ltd, set up in 1995, is a private shareholding firm capitalised at 56.3 million riyals ($15.46 million). It is building a 100-bed hospital where patients will have to pay for services.</p>
<p>The new listing raises market capitalisation on the exchange to 7.47 billion riyals.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.64 riyals)</p>
</text>
